~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Mental Model

Think of React as having three phases:

1. Render Phase
----------------
Run component
Register hooks
Build Virtual DOM

2. Commit Phase
----------------
Update DOM
Run useLayoutEffect

3. Post Commit
----------------
Browser paints
Run useEffect


That's how React "knows" to run effects later: while rendering, it records them in its internal hook/effect lists,
                                               and then executes those lists in the appropriate phase after the DOM work is complete.
